// PostScript grammar — PARG source (parsanol grammar language).
//
// Normative source: the PostScript Language Guide
// (claricle/postscript-guide — https://claricle.github.io/postscript-guide/).
// Coverage contract for this grammar:
//
//   docs/syntax/tokens.adoc        -> lexer rules (tokens, whitespace, comments)
//   docs/syntax/objects.adoc       -> object forms (simple vs composite)
//   docs/syntax/data-types.adoc    -> literal shapes (integer/real/string/hex/name)
//   docs/syntax/strings.adoc       -> literal () strings, <hex> strings, escapes
//   docs/syntax/arrays.adoc        -> [ ... ] array syntax
//   docs/syntax/dictionaries.adoc  -> << ... >> dictionary syntax
//   docs/syntax/procedures.adoc    -> { ... } procedure syntax
//   docs/syntax/operators.adoc     -> operator name rules
//   docs/commands/**               -> the operator vocabulary the grammar
//                                     must accept (300+ operators, per level)
//   docs/levels/*                  -> Level 1/2/3 feature gating
//
// Issue: claricle/postscript#4. Compiles via the parsanol PARG
// toolchain to the artifact the native engine registers:
//
//   parsanol parg compile postscript.parg -o postscript.json
//
// Skeleton below — each commented rule cites the guide page it must
// be developed from:

// program := { ws | comment | literal | operator }
// comment := "%" [^\n]*
// literal := number | string | hex_string | name | array | procedure | dictionary
// operator := <keyword per Model::Operators registry>
